  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PPP training in Cotonou</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public Private Partnerships (PPP) is a new approach for financing infrastructure in Benin. Legislation is currently passing through parliament. International experience has shown that several hurdles must be surmounted before contracts can be commissioned successfully.The port of Cotonou will develop a master plan for its future development with the expertise of Dutch companies Witteveen &amp; Bos, Maritime &amp; Transport Business Solutions (MTBS) and Port of Amsterdam International. The master planning process is highly relevant for Benin and represents a significant investment in the country&apos;s economic performance.Before implementing the master plan, the Port of Cotonou needs to improve the PPP knowledge of its stakeholders. Therefore, this project aims to strengthen their PPP project development and management.</narrative>
  </description>
